# Normalise to LF on commit and on checkout, on every platform.
#
# Everything in this repo is consumed inside Linux containers or by bash on the
# host. A CRLF introduced by a Windows git client does not fail loudly -- it
# fails at runtime, as `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M` on the backup scripts, or
# as a YAML value with a trailing \r that Compose passes through into a
# container environment variable. Pin the behaviour here rather than depend on
# every clone having core.autocrlf set correctly.
#
# Note this cannot protect the executable bit; only a git client that can see
# Unix file modes does that. See the WSL setup notes in the README.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The ones that actually break, stated explicitly so intent survives edits.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
